\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186485721 :question/problem "$\\int 48(3x-13)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 48(3x-13)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186485729 :question/problem "$\\int 18(12-5x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 18(12-5x)^{5}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186485739 :question/problem "$\\int 48(3x-3)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 48(3x-3)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186485746 :question/problem "$\\int 48(3x-1)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 48(3x-1)^{7}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186486406 :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the fractional term $-\\frac{8x}{5}$ by subtracting $3$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{8x}{5}+3 & =5 \\\\ -\\frac{8x}{5}+3-3 & =5-3 \\\\ -\\frac{8x}{5} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe fractional coefficient is $-\\frac{8}{5},$ so we multiply by its reciprocal ${\\left(-\\frac{8}{5}\\right)}^{-1}=-\\frac{5}{8}.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{8x}{5}\\right) & =-\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot 2 \\\\ 1x & =-\\frac{10}{8} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we isolate the fractional term $-\\frac{8x}{5}$ by subtracting $3$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{8x}{5}+3 & =5 \\\\ -\\frac{8x}{5}+3-3 & =5-3 \\\\ -\\frac{8x}{5} & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe fractional coefficient is $-\\frac{8}{5},$ so we multiply by its reciprocal $$\n\\displaystyle {\\left(-\\frac{8}{5}\\right)}^{-1}=-\\frac{5}{8}.\n$$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{8x}{5}\\right) & =-\\frac{5}{8}\\cdot 2 \\\\ 1x & =-\\frac{10}{8} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186486419 :question/worked-solution "First, we isolate the fractional term $-\\frac{2x}{3}$ by subtracting $\\frac{5}{2}$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2x}{3}+\\frac{5}{2} & =4 \\\\ -\\frac{2x}{3}+\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{5}{2} & =\\frac{8}{2}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{2x}{3} & =\\frac{8-5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{2x}{3} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{2x}{3} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe fractional coefficient is $-\\frac{2}{3},$ so we multiply by its reciprocal ${\\left(-\\frac{2}{3}\\right)}^{-1}=-\\frac{3}{2}.$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{2x}{3}\\right) & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1x & =-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "First, we isolate the fractional term $-\\frac{2x}{3}$ by subtracting $\\frac{5}{2}$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2x}{3}+\\frac{5}{2} & =4 \\\\ -\\frac{2x}{3}+\\frac{5}{2}-\\frac{5}{2} & =\\frac{8}{2}-\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{2x}{3} & =\\frac{8-5}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{2x}{3} & =\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{2x}{3} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe fractional coefficient is $-\\frac{2}{3},$ so we multiply by its reciprocal $$\n\\displaystyle {\\left(-\\frac{2}{3}\\right)}^{-1}=-\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$ This gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\left(-\\frac{2x}{3}\\right) & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1x & =-\\frac{9}{4} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186486435 :question/problem "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n=66$ from a population where $42%$ of the population has a particular characteristic. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $i=1,…,66.$ Find an approximate sampling distribution of the statistic $X={\\sum }_{i=1}^{66}{X}_{i}.$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*" "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n=66$ from a population where $42%$ of the population has a particular characteristic. Let the random variable ${X}_{i}$ be equal to\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic} \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $i=1,…,66.$ Find an approximate sampling distribution of the statistic $$\n\\displaystyle X={\\sum }_{i=1}^{66}{X}_{i}.\n$$\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*"] [:db/cas 17592186486542 :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 2 x \\csc^{2}{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 2 x \\csc^{2}{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186486552 :question/problem "Calculate $\\int 2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 2 x \\sin{\\left(x^{2} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186486555 :question/problem "$\\int 8 x^{2} \\sec^{2}{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 8 x^{2} \\sec^{2}{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186486565 :question/problem "What is $\\int 17 {e}^{- 6 x - 2}\\,\\text{d}x$?" "What is $$\n\\displaystyle \\int 17 {e}^{- 6 x - 2}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$?"] [:db/cas 17592186486579 :question/problem "$\\int 17 {e}^{8 x + 3}\\,\\text{d}x=$" "$$\n\\displaystyle \\int 17 {e}^{8 x + 3}\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186486582 :question/problem "Calculate $\\int {e}^{\\frac{x}{7} - 4}\\,\\text{d}x.$" "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int {e}^{\\frac{x}{7} - 4}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186487292 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle {\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{2}}2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\n$$\n{{field-1}}"] [:db/cas 17592186487293 :question/problem "$2\\,Γ\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)+Γ\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)=$" "$$\n\\displaystyle 2\\,Γ\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)+Γ\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)=\n$$"] [:db/cas 17592186487307 :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\